# No DB changes by the agent

The user makes all database changes himself.

- Never run anything that writes to a DB (develop, local, or prod): no ALTER, CREATE, DROP, UPDATE, INSERT, DELETE, or EXEC of a procedure that writes.
- The most the agent may do is write a `.sql` file (e.g. under `Server/shabas-server/sql/`) and tell the user what it does and in which order to run it.
- Read-only SELECT queries (data, `INFORMATION_SCHEMA`, `OBJECT_DEFINITION`) are allowed for investigation.
- Code must keep working before the user runs the script. Treat new columns as optional (e.g. `q.ConnectMode ?? null`).
- SQL files should be safe to run twice: `IF COL_LENGTH(...) IS NULL`, `CREATE OR ALTER`.
